{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Read direct messages"},"description":"Direct messages sent to your Instagram and Facebook accounts, newest conversation first. Call with no argument for the inbox, account_id for one account, or conversation_id for one thread and its messages.\n\nOne conversation is one person on one of your accounts: the platforms carry no thread id, so the person is the thread.\n\nreplyUntil is the deadline for answering and it is the point of this tool. Meta allows a reply within 24 hours of their last message and refuses after it, so a null replyUntil means a reply will be rejected however good it is \u2014 say so rather than drafting one. closesInSeconds counts down to the same moment.\n\nparticipant may be null. The webhook carries ids and no names, so an unnamed person is the platform not saying, not an anonymous one \u2014 do not report them as anonymous.\n\nfromUs marks our own messages, which include replies sent from the platform's own app. A message the sender unsent has gone set and keeps its place, so a reply still reads in order.\n\nThe inbox comes 50 conversations at a time; when nextCursor is not null, pass it as cursor with the same arguments for more.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"account_id":{"description":"One connected account, from accounts_list.","type":"string"},"conversation_id":{"description":"One thread, from a previous messages_list row. Returns its messages oldest first.","type":"string"},"cursor":{"description":"nextCursor from the previous page, for the page after it.","type":"string"},"limit":{"description":"How many conversations to return. Defaults to 50.","maximum":200,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"unread_only":{"description":"Only conversations where they wrote last.","type":"boolean"}},"type":"object"},"name":"messages_list","outputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/d